## Findings

| ID | Sev | Site | Finding | Status |
|----|-----|------|---------|--------|
| M-SG1 / 7.1 | CRIT | `c_guard_scan_idents` | **Undefined** while called from `c_secret_emit_guard` (println/eprintln/log/… and write_file/fetch). Working tree had call sites without a body → link/compile break on those sinks. | **FIXED** — implemented with `str_slice` per ident span |
| M-SG2 / 7.1 | CRIT | same | Per-char `out = out + char_at` would be O(token²) OoStr thrash if naive accumulate used | **FIXED by design** — no char concat; one `str_slice(args, start, i)` per ident |
| M-SG3 / 7.2 | CRIT | `c_sys_exec_last_arg` | Last-arg extract rebuilt with per-char `out = out + char_at` (heap thrash on long shell args) | **FIXED** — `str_slice(args, last_start, n)` |
| M-SG4 | HIGH | `c_args_drop_first` | Same per-char rebuild of remainder after first comma | **FIXED** — `str_slice(args, j, n)` (adjacent easy hygiene) |
| M-SG5 | MED | guard coverage | `c_secret_emit_guard` uses alias-resolved refuse (`c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` / `__alias__` chain ≤16) on sealed sinks | **PASS** (present) |
| M-SG6 | MED | scan string-awareness | Ident walker skips `"..."` / `\\` escapes so string payloads are not false idents | **PASS** (structural) |
| M-SG7 | OPEN | net/FFI sinks | Prior `grok_bottom_up_verify` C5 claimed tcp_write/dlopen via `c_guard_scan_idents` on a1/a2; tip guard has no tcp_write/dlopen branches | **OPEN residual** (T2-class; not in this OWN fix) |
| M-SG8 | OPEN | T1 taint | Secret return / control-flow (2.1, 2.4, 5.1–5.3) not memory-heap; not closed here | **OPEN** (SPRINT T1) |

## Fixes landed (this pass)

### 1. `c_guard_scan_idents` — CRIT 7.1

File: `ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo`

- String-aware linear walk of C arg text (`args`).
- Ident start = `_` / alpha; cont = alnum / `_`.
- **One** `str_slice(args, start, i)` per token, then `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`.
- Aux memory: O(1) scalars (`i`, `in_str`, `start`) + one token slice at a time.
- Time: O(|args|) char visits; no growing concat buffer.

Call sites (unchanged intent):

- println / eprintln / print_err / log / fprintf / syslog → full `args` scan
- write_file / fetch → full `args` scan (complements a1/a2 resolved refuse)

### 2. `c_sys_exec_last_arg` — CRIT 7.2

File: `ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo`

- Replaced per-char rebuild with `str_slice(args, last_start, n)`.
- Scanner still string-/depth-aware for top-level commas (unchanged).

### 3. `c_args_drop_first` — adjacent

- Remainder after first top-level comma via `str_slice(args, j, n)`.

## Complexity claims (memory class)

| Function | Time | Aux heap growth |
|----------|------|-----------------|
| `c_guard_scan_idents` | O(\|args\|) | O(1) temps + O(\|ident\|) per token (slice), no O(n²) concat |
| `c_sys_exec_last_arg` | O(\|args\|) | O(1) + one final slice |
| `c_args_drop_first` | O(\|args\|) | O(1) + one slice |
| `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` | O(1) chain ≤16 | O(1) temps |

Claim: **no per-char OoStr thrash on the OWN paths above.** Residual 7.10 (`c_parse_secret_env` name accumulate via `name = name + c`) remains OPEN elsewhere.

