## Notes (return)

1. **Missing body was the real CRIT:** call sites for `c_guard_scan_idents` landed in the dirty tree without a definition; memory fix is inseparable from defining the walker.
2. **7.1 style = slice, not stack C buffer:** language has no char stack array in `.oo`; correct alpha fix is `str_slice` once per span (avoids OoStr quadratic thrash). Same pattern applied to last-arg (7.2).
3. **Alias resolve stays:** scan → `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` so `let f = secret` style rebinds via `__alias__` still refuse (path-A partial; full 2.4 rebind remains T1).
4. **Did not expand OWN** into tcp_write/dlopen or `c_parse_secret_env` (7.10) — documented OPEN only.
5. No product rebuild / dual-green prove in this pass; code-level memory audit only.

end of t1_memory.oot
